{"title":"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The repeating decimal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f6093e3387a0d96710837bf74e8d6fe48c5daf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.ab\\cdots k\\overline{pq\\cdots u}=\\frac mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"166\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime integers, and there is at least one decimal before the repeating part. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisble by 2 or 5 (or both). (For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc38e714fce751acb7f6bc0de754db85131fb82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.011\\overline{36}=0.01136363636\\cdots=\\frac 1{88}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"267\" height=\"37\" />, and 88 is divisible by 2.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First, split up the nonrepeating parts and the repeating parts of the decimal, so that the nonrepeating parts equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084079bf1d54500f3c59257a7ec3467932b72ba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" /> and the repeating parts of the decimal is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269e8aa087f4751810531fcc03fb551d7030df82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose that the length of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/097bac84f160d0506fb568dd2aeb002d1ca43653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.ab\\cdots k$\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> digits. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06da2803e375c3cb33fbcf3351359afaab916291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b} = \\frac{0.ab\\cdots k}{10^{p+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba94754e4b1493e9ac577cd1a22228aa12d0b5f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.ab\\cdots k &lt; 10^{p+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" />, after reducing the fraction, there MUST be either a factor of 2 or 5 remaining in the denominator. After adding the fractions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f0ad7aa4e79da4e702a3c022aabcc046430f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}+\\frac{c}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" />, the simplified denominator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e4d608a44eab9b604445a6c078ab41ebc4e932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\\\lcm(b,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> has a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must also have a factor of 2 or 5.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>It is well-known that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cda1bc5ad1c9d9b383ce40fcfe4497d4c66a69b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.ab...k \\overline{pq...u} = \\frac{ab...u - ab...k}{99...900...0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"234\" height=\"37\" />, where there are a number of 9s equal to the count of digits in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/6486e9ffa9d342f90c35e0483bd6e91e9331a66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq...u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" />, and there are a number of 0s equal to the count of digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622db7d60b1bee4e31ae6e1dcf397edb1cbad1f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab...k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/2/622db7d60b1bee4e31ae6e1dcf397edb1cbad1f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab...k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/6486e9ffa9d342f90c35e0483bd6e91e9331a66a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq...u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> (which is itself the repeating part), so the numerator cannot have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> consecutive terminating zeros, and hence the denominator still possesses a factor of 2 or 5 not canceled out. This completes the proof.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO\" title=\"1988 USAMO\">1988 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181103\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 175/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4687/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\n